# Copy this file to whitelist.txt and replace the entries below with the
# networks that must never be blocked — your own infrastructure, egress
# ranges, monitoring hosts, VPN concentrators, business-critical partners.
#
# Any block/deny targeting a network that OVERLAPS an entry here is rejected
# outright: no prompt, no database write. A /16 that merely contains one
# whitelisted /32 is rejected too.
#
# If whitelist.txt does not exist, nothing is protected and the tool warns
# on every run.
#
# Format:
#   - One IP, CIDR, or dash range per line (1.1.1.1-1.1.1.26)
#   - Plain IPv4 is treated as /32, plain IPv6 as /64
#   - # starts a comment, inline or full-line
#   - Blank lines ignored; invalid entries warn and are skipped

# --- replace everything below this line ---

# Core infrastructure — never block
203.0.113.0/24      # NOC uplink
198.51.100.10       # monitoring host
2001:db8::/32       # IPv6 management range
